<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84144" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bind</i> or <i>tie the feet</i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to have the feet tied, to be hobbled,</i> of
			horses, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ ταῖς φάτναις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					3.3.27
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ κῶλον ποδισθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					63
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>furnish with feet,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πεποδισμένα ζῷα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
					55
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in Prosody,
				<i>measure by feet, scan,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροχαϊκῶς ποδίζεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					11.37
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>dance</i> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδισμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				219
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
